<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n35930" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">phărē^tra</span></b> , ae,
			f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φαρέτρα</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i>a quiver</i> for
			holding arrows (<b>poet.</b> and late Lat.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">succinctam pharetrā,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 1, 323</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nec venenatis gravida sagittis, Fusce,
					pharetra,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					C. 1, 22, 3</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pharetram solvere,</span>”
				<i>to undo</i>, <i>open</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					5, 379</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">venatricis puellae (Dianae),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Juv.
					13, 80</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in pharetrā suā abscondit
					me,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Isa. 49, 2</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Verg. G. 2, 125</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Prop. 2, 9,
				10</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ov. P. 4, 13, 38</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Am. 3,
				9, 7</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Val. Fl. 3, 607</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Stat. Th.
				4, 259 al.</span></i>— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>a kind of sundial
				in the form of a quiver</i>, <i><span class="en">Vitr. 9, 8,
				1</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
